<%- include("websitepartials/header") %>
<main class="main">
  <!-- Page Title -->
  <div
    class="page-title dark-background"
    style="
      background-image: url(website-assets/img/gallery/Dr-Basilia-Igbokwe3.jpg);
    "
  >
    <div class="container position-relative">
      <h1>Registrar</h1>
      <p>Office of the Registrar</p>
      <nav class="breadcrumbs">
        <ol>
          <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
          <li class="current">Administration</li>
        </ol>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </div>
  <!-- End Page Title -->

  <!-- Alumni Section -->
  <section id="alumni" class="alumni section pb-0">
    <div class="container" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
      <div class="impact-banner" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="200">
        <div class="row align-items-center">
          <div class="col-lg-7">
            <div class="impact-content">
              <h3 class="mb-3">Office of the Registrar</h3>

              <p>
                The Registry is the department concerned with the day-to-day
                administration of the Polytechnic. It derives its functions and
                responsibilities from that of the Registrar as defined in the
                Polytechnic Bye-Law. The Registry is headed by the Registrar,
                who is the Chief Administrative Officer of the Polytechnic.
              </p>

              <p>
                The Registrar as the Head of the Polytechnic Administration,
                under the supervision of the Rector, provides services to enable
                the Polytechnic perform its tripartite function of teaching,
                research and community service by guiding and facilitating the
                work of the various committees constituted for the proper
                running of the Polytechnic. The Registrar facilitates the
                functions of the organs of governance and their committees in
                his capacity as Secretary to the statutory bodies i.e. The
                Governing Council, Congregation and Convocation.
              </p>
              <div class="impact-buttons">
                <a href="/mission-vision-objectives" class="btn-donate"
                  >Our Vision</a
                >
                <a href="/rector-message" class="btn-learn-more"
                  >Rector's Message <i class="bi bi-arrow-right"></i
                ></a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="col-lg-5">
            <div class="impact-image">
              <img
                src="website-assets/img/council/new-registrar.jpg"
                alt="registrar"
                class="img-fluid"
              />
              <div class="impact-stat">
                <i class="bi bi-person-circle me-2"></i>
                <span class="stat-text">Mr. Njoku Stanley Ugochukwu</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="leadership" class="leadership section">
    <div class="container" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
      <div class="row mb-5">
        <div class="col-lg-12" data-aos="fade-right" data-aos-delay="200">
          <h3 class="section-subtitle mb-3">Profile of the Registrar</h3>
          <div class="stats-container">
            <p>
              Mr. Njoku Stanley Ugochukwu is the current Registrar of the DR.
              B.U. NZERIBE STATE POLYTECHNIC, AWO-OMAMMA, Owerri. He officially
              assumed office on January 11, 2025, following his appointment by
              the institution’s Governing Council after a transparent and
              merit-based selection process.
            </p>

            <p>
              Before his appointment, Mr. Njoku served as Deputy Registrar at
              the Federal University of Technology, Owerri (FUTO), where he
              built a reputation as a seasoned and dedicated administrator. His
              experience in tertiary institution management positioned him as an
              ideal candidate to steer the Registry Department of the
              Polytechnic.
            </p>

            <p>
              As Registrar, Mr. Njoku functions as the Chief Administrative
              Officer of the Polytechnic, overseeing the operations of the
              Registry Department. He also serves as Secretary to key statutory
              bodies of the institution, including the Governing Council,
              Congregation, and Convocation, playing a central role in policy
              implementation and institutional governance.
            </p>

            <p>
              Mr. Njoku’s tenure is expected to reflect his strong commitment to
              professionalism, transparency, and administrative innovation,
              aligning with the Polytechnic’s vision for excellence in
              institutional management.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <!-- /Leadership Section -->
</main>

<%- include("websitepartials/footer") %>
